{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_32790b7ead9a4948841858e4a3aa090513de616cf7c825c12f7e994a99e8dde0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Desktop GUI business capabilities enter the Rust runtime only through App Server JSON-RPC; Electron IPC is limited to windows, file selection, system permissions, notifications, updates, native views, and sidecar lifecycle."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4b77d48813e64244206c481d888475847d7b5130b866fd7c5fa9ba36891006f1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: minimal documentation checks are `npm run docs:boundary`, relative-link validation, and `git diff --check`, with `npm run governance:legacy-report` added when governance categories change."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5a540c3290e1bd6954b0a094e070993e17536264b22f78f2b71e9b3608ef4c9d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"FEATURE-MAP assigns ownership across crates: agent-runtime/agent for turn lifecycle and orchestration, model-provider for catalog/routing/retry, and tool-runtime for tool definitions, permissions, sandbox, dispatch, processes and MCP; the main-chain diagram lists thread-store/repository for persistence and projection."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8d04121bcac26cde224365e9233ca72c37ffa60e7e9ebdac20347af6a2c36cc5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: FEATURE-MAP maintenance rules require updating code and the architecture doc first, then syncing the map after owner confirmation, and readiness is judged by code, protocol, and corresponding evidence levels rather than roadmap claims or single test results."}],"claim_ids":["clm_32790b7ead9a4948841858e4a3aa090513de616cf7c825c12f7e994a99e8dde0","clm_4b77d48813e64244206c481d888475847d7b5130b866fd7c5fa9ba36891006f1","clm_5a540c3290e1bd6954b0a094e070993e17536264b22f78f2b71e9b3608ef4c9d","clm_8d04121bcac26cde224365e9233ca72c37ffa60e7e9ebdac20347af6a2c36cc5"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_f60ceac5823a43ef90794993c02d7e75","id":"pg_2a6a27579af